description:'Create a new page in a specified Confluence space.\n\nThis tool creates a new page, which is the primary content type for collaboration, documentation, and knowledge sharing in Confluence. To create a page, you must provide a title, the ID and name of the space it belongs to, and the page content in \'Storage\' format (e.g., HTML) or \'AtlasDocFormat\'. You can optionally specify a parent page to create a nested page structure. When specifying a parent page, both `ParentId` and `ParentTitle` must be provided.\n\nAggressively resolve all missing parameters that reference existing information by exhausting your search tools, and only ask the user for clarification on subjective choices or new content that you cannot possibly infer.\n\nRaises\n------\nInvalidIdentifierError\n    Raised if the provided \'SpaceId\' or \'ParentId\' is invalid or not found.\nPermissionError\n    Raised when the user lacks permission to create a page in the specified space.\nContentFormatError\n    Raised if the content provided in \'Storage\' or \'AtlasDocFormat\' is malformed.\n\nUsage Examples\n--------------\nNote that parameters are passed in together as an object if parameters need to be passed in.\nTo create a new page titled "New Team Meeting Notes" in space \'8675309\':\n    create_page(SpaceId="8675309", SpaceName="My Space", Storage="<p>This is the content of our new page.</p><ul><li>Item 1</li><li>Item 2</li></ul>", Title="New Team Meeting Notes")\n\nSample successful response:\n```json\n{\n  "id": "123457",\n  "title": "New Team Meeting Notes",\n  "spaceId": "8675309",\n  "status": "current",\n  "parentId": null,\n  "version": {\n    "number": 1,\n    "message": ""\n  }\n}\n```\n\nTo create a new draft page titled "Q4 Planning Draft" as a child of page \'123456\' with title \'Parent Page Title\' in space \'8675309\':\n    create_page(ParentId=123456, ParentTitle="Parent Page Title", SpaceId="8675309", SpaceName="My Space", Status="draft", Storage="<h1>Q4 Goals</h1><p>Initial thoughts and planning for the upcoming quarter.</p>", Title="Q4 Planning Draft")\n\nSample successful response:\n```json\n{\n  "id": "123458",\n  "title": "Q4 Planning Draft",\n  "spaceId": "8675309",\n  "status": "draft",\n  "parentId": "123456",\n  "version": {\n    "number": 1,\n    "message": ""\n  }\n}\n```\n\nDependencies\n------------\n- The search tool and get_space tool: These two tools can be used jointly to find the \'SpaceId\' required to create a page. \n- list_spaces: Lists all available Spaces in Confluence. This tool can be used to find the \'SpaceId\' required to create a page in a specific space.',
