ults by. If not provided, issues are sorted by \'created\' date by default.\n    Examples: "priority", "dueDate"\nmaxResults: integer, optional\n    The maximum number of issues to return per page. If not specified, defaults to 50.\n    Examples: 25, 100\nnextPageToken: string, optional\n    An optional page token to fetch the next page of results, used for pagination when the total number of issues exceeds `maxResults`.\n\nReturns\n-------\nissues: array\n    A list of issue objects matching the JQL query. Each object contains fields like: url, key, title, status, project_name, description, entity_type, due_date, priority, creator_name, creator_email, reporter_name, reporter_email, assignee_name, assignee_email, url_for_connector, issue_id, issue_key, project_id, project_key, issue_type, created, updated.\n    Examples: `[{\\"id\\": \\"10021\\", \\"key\\": \\"PROJ-123\\", \\"title\\": \\"Login button not working\\", \\"assignee_name\\": \\"John Doe\\"}, {\\"id\\": \\"10022\\", \\"key\\": \\"PROJ-124\\", \\"summary\\": \\"Update user profile page\\", \\"assignee_name\\": \\"John Doe\\"}]`\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError\n    Raised if the \'query\' parameter contains invalid JQL syntax.\nPermissionError\n    Raised if the user lacks the necessary permissions to view the issues or projects specified in the filter.\n\nUsage Examples\n--------------\nNote that parameters are passed in together as an object if parameters need to be passed in.\nTo list issues for project \'PROJ\':\n    search_issues(query="project = PROJ")\nTo list issues assigned to the current user that are \'In Progress\', sorted by priority:\n    search_issues(query="assignee = currentUser() AND status = \'In Progress\'", sort_by="priority")\nTo find all issues that have a due date in 2024 and are assigned to \'John Doe\':\n    search_issues(query="due >= 2024-01-01 AND due <= 2024-12-31 AND assignee = \\"John Doe\\"")',
