dataSourceName:"outlook_federated_eua",dataConnectorName:"",relatedEntityName:"Events"},{name:"send_mail",displayName:"",iconUrl:"https://gstatic.com/vertexaisearch/icons/64px/outlook.png",description:'Send an email message from the authenticated user\'s Office 365 mailbox.\n\nThis tool allows for sending emails in two primary ways: composing a new message from scratch or sending an existing draft message.\n\nTo compose and send a new email, you must provide the `ToRecipients` parameter and at least one of `Subject` or `Content`. You can also include CC/Bcc recipients, a body with a specified content type, and attachments.\n\nAlternatively, to send a pre-existing draft message, provide its unique `Id`. When the `Id` is used, all other composition-related parameters like `Subject`, `Content`, or `ToRecipients` are ignored.\n\nAggressively resolve all missing parameters that reference existing information by exhausting your search tools, and only ask the user for clarification on subjective choices or new content that you cannot possibly infer.\n\nRaises\n------\nError\n    - Raised if recipient email addresses are invalid or cannot be resolved.\n    - Raised if the provided `Id` for a draft message does not exist or is not a draft.\n    - Raised if the user lacks the necessary permissions to send from the specified `FromEmail` or on behalf of the `SenderEmail`.\n\nUsage Examples\n--------------\nNote that parameters are passed in together as an object if parameters need to be passed in.\nTo send a new email with a subject and body to multiple recipients:\n    send_mail(CCRecipients="manager@example.com", Content="Here are the notes from today\'s meeting.", ContentType="text", Subject="Meeting Follow-up", ToRecipients="user1@example.com;user2@example.com")\nTo send an existing draft email using its ID:\n    send_mail(Id="AAMkADkzZDg2ZTEzLTQwY2YtNDU5Ni05ZTJlLTYzZGY4Y2E4MzkyYQBGAAAAAAD...")\nTo send a new email with multiple attachments, if the file content is not base64 encoded, the tool will automatically base64 encode the string content:\n    send_mail(Attachments="Q3-Report.pdf,SGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=;notes.txt,SGVsbG8gd29ybGQ=", Content="Please review the attached files.", Subject="Q3 Report and Notes", ToRecipients="jane.doe@example.com")\nTo send a new email with an attachment from a string, string content should be base64 encoded. If not, the tool will automatically base64 encode the string content.:\n    send_mail(Content="Please see the attached file.", ContentBytes="SGVsbG8gV29ybGQh.", FileName="attachment.txt", Subject="Text file attachment", ToRecipients="jane.doe@example.com")\n\nDependencies\n------------\nThis tool depends on the following services:\n    Office 365: This tool interacts with the Office 365 platform to send email messages.',
